# Markdown formatting

## Tables

Apply when creating or editing GFM tables in `.md` / `.mdc`, and in Markdown tables inside `.yaml` / `.yml` (including commented tables, e.g. `.coderabbit.yaml`).

### Separator row — always short

Use minimal hyphens. Do **not** pad separators to match header width.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
| Step | kind | Details |
|---|---|---|

<!-- ❌ BAD — padded separators -->
| Step | kind | Details |
|------|------|---------|
```

### Cells — exactly one space around content

One space after `|` and one space before the next `|`. No column padding / alignment spaces.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
| Step | kind | Details |
|---|---|---|
| collectForm | collectForm | `Email` (required). → `createUser` |

<!-- ❌ BAD — extra spaces for column alignment -->
| Step        | kind        | Details                          |
| ----------- | ----------- | -------------------------------- |
| collectForm | collectForm | `Email` (required). → `createUser` |
```

### Pipe bookends

Every table line (header, separator, body) **must** start and end with `|`.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
| A | B |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |

<!-- ❌ BAD — missing leading or trailing pipe -->
A | B |
---|---
| 1 | 2
```

### Empty cells

Exactly **one** space between pipes. Not empty `||`, not two spaces `|  |`.

```markdown
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
| | |
| A | |

<!-- ❌ BAD -->
|  |  |
|| ||
```
